            <ArticleTitle>Giant left anterior descending coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e27-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Small atherosclerotic coronary artery aneurysms are a relatively frequent incidental finding at angiography. We report an unusual case in that the aneurysm found was extremely large and therefore potentially at risk of rupture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
